Yes, fixed in 3.4.3.  I will explain it, but if you ever post a YAAP
here using the exploit, you'll be considered an outcast!  Fair
warning...

Anyway, once you get a wand of wishing, you can burn a wish for, say,
3 cursed loadstones.  Now, adjust your inventory so that the wand of
wishing is in the next inventory slot after the loadstones.  If the
loadstones are in slot j, #adjust the wand of wishing to k.  Next,
drop n-1 loadstones.  "For some reason, you cannot drop the stones!"

All well, and good, but check your inventory.  You now have 1
loadstone and n wands of wishing.  Essentially, there was a bug in
which n-1 items were taken out of inventory slot j in the normal drop
routine.  This routine returned failure, as you can't drop cursed
loadstones, but the n-1 items were put back into inventory slot k, not
j.  This apparently only happened when dropping part of a stack of
items.  Note that this technique works equally well to multiply
artifacts (of which there should only ever be one!)

Now that you know, forget you ever heard it! :)

